          %title Logarithms
          %h1#logarithms Logarithms
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#logarithms_of_real_numbers"} Logarithms of real numbers
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#logarithms_of_complex_numbers"} Logarithms of complex numbers
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#logarithms_and_lie_groups"} Logarithms and Lie groups
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Classically, a logarithm is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partially-defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+map"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            from a multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/numbers"} numbers
            to an additive group of numbers. As such, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+section"} local section
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+map"} exponential map
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#logarithms_of_real_numbers Logarithms of real numbers
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            under addition (which we will call simply
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^*
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+component"} identity component
            (which we will call
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^+
          %p
            The Lie groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^+
            are in fact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            other than
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^+
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            is called the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                real logarithm with base
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi log
                      %mi b
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \log_b x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^+
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                real
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+map"} exponential map
                with base
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto b^x
          %p
            The real logarithms are handily defined using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+integral"} Riemann integral
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reciprocal"} reciprocal
            as follows:
          #eq:integrals.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ln
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ∫
                            %mn 1
                            %mi x
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mi t
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %mi t
                          %mo ;
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi log
                            %mi b
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi ln
                              %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %mi ln
                              %mi b
                          %mo .
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  \\ln x &amp; \coloneqq \int_1^x \frac{1}{t} \,\mathrm{d}t ;\\
                  \\log_b x &amp; \coloneqq \frac{\ln x}{\ln b} .\\
                  }
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ln
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ln
            is itself a logarithm, the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong natural logarithm
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2.71828182845
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e} = 2.71828182845\ldots
          %h3#logarithms_of_complex_numbers Logarithms of complex numbers
          %p
            Now consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            under addition (which we call
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^*
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+space"} connected
          %p
            However,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^*
            are
            %em not
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo *
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^* \times S^1 \to \mathbb{C}^*
          %p
            exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^*
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
            (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^*
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^* \to \mathbb{C}
            are given by pairs of homomorphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^* \to \mathbb{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon S^1 \to \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon S^1 \to \mathbb{C}
            is trivial: the restriction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion subgroup
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            is trivial since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            is torsionfree, and since the torsion subgroup is dense in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
